column119:
22/Nov/12 4:26 PM;557058:a04c228c-7d70-4967-8583-25de929b4720;pullreq: https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/pull/989

changes:
 - Added a case in CSS cleaner to remove value "fixed" for property "position"
 - Added two rules, "overflow: hidden" and "position: relative" to style for #workskin,
to prevent elements inside works from overflowing out of the work container


test notes:

Make a work skin like this:
---
div { padding: 15px; }

.bsod {
  background: #00f;
  color: #fff;
  height: 100%;
  left: 0;
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  width: 100%;
  z-index: 999;
}

.escapee {
  background: #0f0;
  left: -10px;
  position: absolute;
  top: -10px;
}
---

And make a work like this:
---
<div class="bsod">OH NOES BSOD</div>

<div class="escapee">i am getting awaaaaay</div>
---

Set the work to use your work skin, then view the work and check that:
- The whole page isn't blue.
- The bright green box is cut off by the boundaries of the work container, and doesn't
overflow outside the container.- **Status changed**: `SubmittedPullRequest`

