column27:
Originally reported on Google Code with ID 3837
What archive revision are you testing on? (See the version label in
the footer, for example v0.8.13.8.)
0.9.11.6

If appropriate, enter the URL of a page where the problem can be seen:

What steps will reproduce the problem?
1. Log in
2. Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Skin
3. Enter a unique Title
4. For CSS, enter: /* my css */ body { background: yellow; } 
5. Submit

What is the expected output? What do you see instead?
I expect my comment to remain in the CSS, so I would see
/* my css */
body {
  background: yellow;
}

Instead, it strips comments and I only see
body {
  background: yellow;
}

Breaking off from Issue 2834

column138:
23/May/20 10:33 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;{quote}
Synning Canonical 1 to Canonical 2 leads to subtags being removed from Canonical 1's wrangling page, since they're now subtags of Canonical 2. This is expected behavior. However, if the syn is undone, the subtags can't always be reassociated to Canonical 1.
{quote}
Nothing prevents a tag being made subtags to multiple canonicals. We should be good.

column128:
16/May/23 8:17 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;{quote}Please also check that the "invited" link in the confirmation message you get when inviting someone else's work to your collection goes to the correct page!{quote}

I invited a work by another user to my (Open, Moderated) collection and got the message:

{quote}This work has been [invited|https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/tz_test_1201/items?status=unreviewed_by_user] to your collection (What timezone am I in?).{quote}

Where “invited” is the expected link: [https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/tz_test_1201/items?status=unreviewed_by_user|https://test.archiveofourown.org/collections/tz_test_1201/items?status=unreviewed_by_user] (the “Awaiting User Approval“ tab, showing that the invitation is “approved by moderation collectors” but “unreviewed by creator“). Looks good.

column121:
12/May/17 10:15 PM;557058:443ab871-4096-403e-bd6f-f3534fe417f0;There's a small change to this in the Rails 4 upgrade

Before:

{code:java}
visible_bookmarks = @collection.approved_bookmarks.visible(order: 'RAND()').limit(ArchiveConfig.NUMBER_OF_ITEMS_VISIBLE_IN_DASHBOARD * 2)
{code}

After:

{code:java}
visible_bookmarks = @collection.approved_bookmarks.visible.order('RAND()').limit(ArchiveConfig.NUMBER_OF_ITEMS_VISIBLE_IN_DASHBOARD * 2)
{code}


When that's deployed to staging, it might be worth giving it a poke and seeing if this issue is any better.

